<release date="2022-09-19" version="2.41" title="Backup Annotations">
    <release-core-list>
        <release-bug-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="1852"/>
                <github-pull-request id="1854"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="adam.brusselback"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stefan.fercot"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Fix incorrect time expiration being used for non-default repositories.</p>

                <p>When <cmd>expire</cmd> ran without <br-option>repo</br-option>, the time-based <br-option>repo-retention-full</br-option> for every repository was read from the lowest-numbered repository. Each repository now uses its own value.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="1870"/>
                <github-pull-request id="1871"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="efremov.egor"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Fix issue when listing directories recursively with a filter.</p>

                <p><cmd>repo-ls</cmd> with <br-option>recurse</br-option> and <br-option>filter</br-option> could fail with a double free or segfault when the last entry in a directory was a directory that had entries. A parent list was freed before the entries of its subdirectories were processed.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-bug-list>

        <release-feature-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="1709"/>
                <github-pull-request id="1724"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="adam.berlin"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="stefan.fercot"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Backup key/value annotations.</p>

                <p>Add key/value annotations to a backup with the <br-option>annotation</br-option> option of the <cmd>backup</cmd> command, and add, modify, or remove them later with the new <cmd>annotate</cmd> command. The <cmd>info</cmd> command shows annotations in text output when <br-option>set</br-option> is specified and always includes them in JSON output.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-feature-list>

        <release-improvement-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="1484"/>
                <github-pull-request id="1501"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="anton.kurochkin"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="stefan.fercot"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Support <br-option>--set</br-option> in JSON output for <cmd>info</cmd> command.</p>

                <p>With <br-option>set</br-option>, JSON output from <cmd>info</cmd> now includes the details that text output already showed, e.g. the error and tablespace lists.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <commit subject="Allow quote tag in command-line help."/>
                <commit subject="Allow upload chunk size to be configured for object stores.">
                    <github-issue id="1843"/>
                    <github-pull-request id="1847"/>
                </commit>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="anton.glushakov"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stefan.fercot"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Allow upload chunk size to be configured for object stores.</p>

                <p>Set <br-option>repo-storage-upload-chunk-size</br-option> to change the size of each upload chunk for S3, GCS, or Azure. Larger chunks can improve performance but use more memory. The defaults are unchanged.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="1853"/>
                <github-pull-request id="1855"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="alex.richman"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stefan.fercot"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Update archive.info timestamps after a successful backup.</p>

                <p><file>archive.info</file> and its copy were written only by <cmd>stanza-create</cmd> and <cmd>stanza-upgrade</cmd>, and an object store lifecycle policy that expires old files could remove them. Their timestamps are now updated after each successful backup.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="1816"/>
                <github-pull-request id="1819"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="keith.fiske"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stefan.fercot"/>
                    <release-item-tester id="keith.fiske"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Move standby timeline check after checkpoint.</p>

                <p>The check that the standby is on the expected timeline used <file>pg_control</file> as it was before the backup started. Right after a promotion the standby may not have written the new timeline to <file>pg_control</file> yet, and the backup failed with <quote>standby is on timeline ... but expected ...</quote>. The check now runs after the checkpoint.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="cynthia.shang"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Improve warning message on backup resume.</p>

                <p>The warning read as if the user needed to take action. It now states that invalid files will be removed and then the backup will resume.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-improvement-list>

